Then solve Data structures and Algorithms problems from GeeksforGeeks Courses | Practice | GeeksforGeeks . In the problems corner, put the topic tag like arrays and solve some 15-20 questions on that topic. Spend around 2-3 months just on geeksforgeeks and slowly cover all the topics as follows: Arrays, Binary Search, Linked Lists, Stacks, Queues, Greedy, Recursion, Trees, DP, and Graphs along with C++ STL (if you use C++). Some tips:
If you get stuck on any question, see the solution to that question and learn and improve your mistakes (Nowadays video solutions are also available on youtube for most of the questions).
Write down important questions/concepts/algorithms in a notebook as it helps in revision later.
Reducing time and space complexities is the most important task once you have solved a question because, in interviews, most of the candidates can solve the question using basic approaches but you are judged on how efficient your approach is.
Initially, you might have difficulty in solving most of the questions, it happens with everyone. But stay there and don’t give up. Think about why you were not able to solve that question, learn from the solution, and keep trying and improving. Success takes time and constant efforts (Pro tip: Spend at least half an hour to think of a solution to a question).
After point 2, a lot of your job is done. But to be super prepared, open Interviewbit. Go to the programming section and start solving questions just like you did on geeksforgeeks. I am assuming until here, you must have solved some 100-150 questions on geeksforgeeks, so now you won’t have much problem in moving to Interviewbit. Solve questions on Interviewbit covering all the topics following the same approach of writing down important questions/concepts/algorithms in a notebook and keep revising things from this notebook from time to time. You will realize that DS/Algo is very similar to Physics/Maths problems ;)
Here your Data Structures and Algorithms preparation is done, which consists of atleast 75% of your interview process. Till here you must have solved 300+ questions of DS/Algo.